        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "sentences. But it is not less difficult to read than many paragraphs made up of longer sentences with multiple independent clauses. We have chosen to punctuate as a series of separate sentences what might have been punctuated as one long one. The period before but, for example, could have been a comma. The last two periods could have been semicolons. And that period could have been a dash.",
            "block_bbox": [
                126,
                117,
                756,
                242
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 2,
            "global_block_id": 2,
